                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00001         ********************************************************************
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00002         * telnet - telnet client
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00003         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00004         * Notes:
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00005         * This utility works in similar fashion to telnet commands on other systems.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00006         * The user can telnet to a location, and once there, press the TELESCAPE key
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00007         * to invoke telnet command mode.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00008         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00009         * Two sets of path options are kept for the standard input.  The first is an
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00010         * unmodified copy and the second is a modifable copy.  The second is set up
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00011         * for raw mode and is used when communicating with the host.  The first will
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00012         * be used when going into telnet command mode or exiting the telnet program.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00013         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00014         * The signal handler catches the S$HUP signal and shuts down gracefully.  It
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00015         * also looks for the ABORT/QUIT characters and relays them to the session.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00016         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00017         * Reference used: http://www.faqs.org/rfcs/rfc854.html
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00018         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00019         * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00020         * Comment
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00021         * ------------------------------------------------------------------
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00022         *   1      2010/01/02  Aaron Wolfe
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00023         * Most basic implementation using new DW utility API
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00024         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00025         *   2      2010/01/06  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00026         * Reformatted and optimized source. Added SS.Opt support, added telnet
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00027         * command mode which can be entered by pressing the TELESCAPE key.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00028         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00029         *   3      2010/01/07  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00030         * Reworked buffer processing routine.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00031         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00032         *   4      2010/01/12  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00033         * We allow host to do echo if it wants, we also now advertise the
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00034         * escape character when a connection is successful.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00035         *
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00036         *   5      2010/01/15  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00037         * Modified to be an rma assembled module and use the netlib library.
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00038         
                      (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00039         * Set to 1 if you want to see telnet CTRL chars from host
     0000             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00040         DEBUG               set       0
