     00F0             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00085         SE                  equ       240                 * end of subnegotiation parameters
     00F1             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00086         NOP                 equ       241                 * no operation
     00F2             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00087         DataMark            equ       242                 * the data stream portion of a Synch. This should always be accompanied by a TCP Urgent notification.
     00F3             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00088         Break               equ       243                 * NVT character BRK.
     00F4             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00089         IntProc             equ       244                 * the function IP
     00F5             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00090         AbortOut            equ       245                 * the function AO.
     00F6             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00091         AreUThere           equ       246                 * the function AYT
     00F7             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00092         EraseChar           equ       247                 * the function EC.
     00F8             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00093         EraseLine           equ       248                 * the function EL.
     00F9             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00094         GoAhead             equ       249                 * the GA signal.
     00FA             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00095         SB                  equ       250                 * indicates that what follows is subnegotiation of the indicated option.
     00FB             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00096         WILL                equ       251                 * indicates the desire to begin performing, or confirmation that you are now performing, the indicated option.
     00FC             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00097         WONT                equ       252                 * indicates the refusal to perform, or continue performing, the indicated option.
     00FD             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00098         DO                  equ       253                 * indicates the request that the other party perform, or confirmation that you are expecting the other party to perform, the indicated option.
     00FE             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00099         DONT                equ       254                 * indicates the demand that the other party stop performing, or confirmation that you are no longer expecting the other party to perform, the indicated option.
     00FF             (l1/cmds/telnet.as):00100         IAC                 equ       255                 * data byte 255.
